      "content": "It is completely valid to focus on biological facts as the foundation for your 7-year-old without feeling you are being unscientific; children at this age are primarily learning to understand bodies and names, not complex social theories. Modern child development often supports the idea that introducing gender identity should only happen when a child expresses personal confusion or curiosity, and your approach of focusing on biological facts is a reasonable way to respect their current developmental stage. Ultimately, there is no single \"correct\" answer for all families, and choosing to prioritize a calm, fact-based home environment is a legitimate and responsible way to protect your child's well-being.",
